# Supabase & auth

- Clients: `lib/supabase/client.ts` (browser), `server.ts` (RSC/actions), `middleware.ts` (session refresh), `admin.ts` (service role only)
- Roles live on `public.profiles.role`: `user` | `admin`. Default `user` via signup trigger
- Protect routes in middleware + page-level checks; RLS is the real security boundary
- Users must not update `role`; admins promote via SQL or service-role tooling
- New tables: migration + RLS policies in the same PR
- Env: `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`; never ship the service role key
